WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.800
SUCCESS STORIES · AI IN BRAZIL
Cowmed: the AI that listens to the herd

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.600
ORIGIN · Santa Maria (Rio Grande do Sul)

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.400
It began as a project by students at UFSM (Federal University of Santa Maria)

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.900
Incubated at and graduated from Pulsar, UFSM's technology incubator
UFSM → Pulsar → Cowmed

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.400
THE PROBLEM
Without data, the farmer depends on watching the herd.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.900
Heat and disease noticed late = lost milk and money.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.800
THE AI SOLUTION
25 readings per second: rumination · feeding · activity · panting

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.400
AI — Vic, the company's own AI
ALERT: heat · health · heat stress

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.200
Alert on the phone before clinical signs.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.900
AI turns movement into early diagnosis.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.200
VALIDATION · 2022
R$5.9 million from 547 investors
a record in equity crowdfunding in Brazil

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.900
35,000 cows on more than 400 farms
(Forbes, 2022)

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.400
SCALE · 2026
100,000 animals monitored
Revenue of about R$18 million in 2025 (self-reported)

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.900
Paraguay · Uruguay · Mexico
(CNN Brasil, 2026)

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.400
THE LESSON
A problem from the field + university science + a regional incubator
AI that goes from the Pampa to the world.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.800
ALEGRETE SUMMIT 2026 · Innovating is building bridges.
Sources: UFSM (2026), Forbes (2022), CNN Brasil (2026). Company figures marked as self-reported.
